A persona this build ships, seeded as a file you own
===================================================

The edition now carries the public Nora persona (42 KB, the edition that passes its own scrub gates:
no personal identifiers, no third parties' names, no pronouns for strangers). It is bundled in
`resources/persona/nora-public.md` rather than fetched, because a persona that arrives over the
network is one you cannot read before it runs.

**Seeded, not baked in.** On first run the engine writes it to `<data_dir>/persona.md` if that file
does not exist. It is a file on disk from that moment — editable, inspectable, and pointed at by the
same path the Persona page shows. Existing installs are untouched: a persona you have written is
never overwritten.

**Restore is explicit.** The Persona page gets one extra button, "Use the shipped persona", which
asks for confirmation first and then replaces the file via `AppPreferences.restoreShippedPersona`.
Nothing on boot ever calls it.
